+# Qualified publication of Judiciary PR #32 — October 23, 2026
+
+This directory holds byte-exact, **non-operative source snapshots** of the
+two four-row correction histories proposed in Viche PR #32, at exact head
+`c140eb3d65e66c97846822788291a5dc2bed7155`. Their file hashes and
+original proposed paths are in `MANIFEST.json`; names end in
+`.proposed.source.txt` rather than `.jsonl` to keep them **out of the
+authoritative correction trail**.
+
+The eight historical Judiciary report documents are published under
+`records/AUDIT-*.md` (except the first, which was already on main). The
+independent second-office factual review, signed as `896a1a36`, is
+published at `records/PR32-SECOND-OFFICE-FACTUAL-REVIEW-2026-10-23.md`.
+That review found an apparent violation of Act 17's one-correction-per-case
+per six-hour cycle limit: each case had two corrective filings about
+65 minutes apart with no recorded distinct cycle. It also found date/time
+discrepancies in historical narratives. These defects must remain visible;
+the historical reports are attributed evidence, NOT an assertion of
+independent corroboration, current correctness or legal compliance.
+
+Prior untracked three-row source versions are already preserved and
+Git-anchored at `records/oversight/source-evidence/2026-10-23/*.source.txt`
+by merge `f21ab85`; there are also durable state backups. Neither
+historical variant is discarded or overwritten.
+
+**Explicit authority boundary:** The files in this directory do not
+authorize or implement Act 17 corrections. The operative files under
+`records/oversight/corrections/*.jsonl` stay unchanged/unpublished.
+PR #32 remains review-blocked for those changes pending independent
+legal interpretation or a valid legislative remedy. Only a subsequently
+approved, independently reviewed, exact-commit-verified change may
+anchor effective corrections to that operative path.
+
+Publication here changes no law, bill, ballot or operational system.
